const PAGE_HTML = "<h1>ShootFlow Business Plan (Working Draft)</h1>\n<p>This is a practical operating plan for turning ShootFlow from a personal tool\ninto a viable software business for high-volume photographers/videographers.</p>\n<h2>1) Core problem and value</h2>\n<p>Target users are spending either:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>direct time (roughly 10-20 hours/week) on ingest, culling, color consistency,\nand social packaging, or</li>\n<li>direct money ($100-$1,000+/week) on outsourced editing and coordination.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>ShootFlow&#39;s value proposition:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Reduce time spent on repetitive post-production operations.</li>\n<li>Increase weekly content throughput (reels, carousels, graded photo sets).</li>\n<li>Preserve quality and consistency through deterministic scene/look pipelines.</li>\n<li>Reduce operational risk with non-destructive ingest and explicit manifests.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2) Initial ICP and wedge</h2>\n<h2>Initial ICP (v1)</h2>\n<p>Professional photographers/videographers and small studios with recurring\nclient delivery pressure:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>wedding/event teams,</li>\n<li>portrait/editorial studios,</li>\n<li>real-estate/media teams with recurring weekly turnaround.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Wedge</h2>\n<p>&quot;Card dump to organized, graded, IG-ready draft package with safety guarantees.&quot;</p>\n<p>Why this wedge wins:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>It solves operational pain before perfect AI creativity is required.</li>\n<li>It is measurable (hours saved, faster turnaround, more deliverables/week).</li>\n<li>It differentiates against pure editing tools that ignore ingest/file safety.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>3) Product scope by phase</h2>\n<h2>Phase 1: trusted automation core (current direction)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>SD/SSD/local source discovery and route recommendation.</li>\n<li>Typed native macOS volume metadata handoff for more accurate ejectable,\nremovable, read-only, network, and system-volume filtering before route review.</li>\n<li>Safe ingest with checksums and immutable manifests.</li>\n<li>Read-only post-ingest production reports that show asset counts, planned\nparallel work, and IG deliverables before downstream jobs write artifacts.</li>\n<li>A single card-dump workflow command that ties route discovery, capacity\ngating, ingest preview, optional confirmed copy, and post-ingest production\nreporting together for Mac app shells and demos, plus a synthetic\ncard-dump-to-render smoke workspace that proves the same path without real\nmedia.</li>\n<li>Resumable <code>production_status.json</code> initialization for pre-render proxy,\nanalysis, grading, storyline, and packaging work, bound to the verified\nmanifest-backed production plan, plus a status-backed next-wave handoff so\nworkers can resume from durable succeeded/running/failed/retryable state\ninstead of trusting caller-reported completion lists.</li>\n<li>Production-worker action/status helpers that plan dependency-ready jobs from\ntrusted status, claim a matching attempt, verify declared outputs before\nsuccess, and report retry/failure without cleanup or deletion authority.</li>\n<li>A deterministic dry-run production adapter that persists claim and result\ntransitions through <code>production_status.json</code>, writes only declared placeholder\nfile outputs, and preserves directory-style package outputs or output\nconflicts as retryable review states before real proxy/VLM/color/story workers\nare introduced.</li>\n<li>A deterministic local package production adapter that verifies trusted\nstoryline plus graded dependency outputs and writes declared package handoff\nartifacts for reel, carousel, and photo-set jobs. Directory-style packages use\na controlled <code>package_manifest.json</code> plus deterministic directory checksums so\npilot dashboards can count materialized first-draft packages without granting\ncleanup, deletion, or arbitrary export authority. Unexpected existing package\ndirectory entries are surfaced by relative name in retryable status/report\nmessages without deleting or trusting those stray bytes.</li>\n<li>A local metadata production adapter that uses the same claim/result boundary\nbut reads trusted local inputs, records file size and SHA-256 metadata, and\nwrites deterministic JSON only to declared output files. This creates a first\nreal input-fingerprint path for proxy/analysis/color/story work without\ngranting copy, overwrite, cleanup, deletion, or arbitrary materialization\nauthority.</li>\n<li>A local proxy production adapter that uses the same guarded boundary to\nbyte-copy trusted local source inputs into declared proxy outputs. This is not\nfinal ffmpeg/Metal proxy generation; it is a safety-proven stand-in that\nexercises real media-byte materialization, checksum success reporting, and\nno-overwrite review behavior before quality-focused proxy rendering is wired\nin.</li>\n<li>A local analysis production adapter that uses the same guarded boundary to\nwrite deterministic, schema-compatible <code>vlm_asset_analysis</code> JSON from trusted\nlocal inputs. This is not final AI understanding; it is a contract probe that\nproves scheduler stage routing, analysis output checksums, and downstream\nloader compatibility before local or hosted VLM workers are trusted.</li>\n<li>A dry-run production scheduler/CLI command that advances trusted pre-render\njobs from <code>production_status.json</code> with bounded parallelism, explicit\ncomplete/blocked/retryable/failed/waiting state, and no cleanup or deletion\nauthority. Previously retryable jobs require an explicit reviewed retry ID\nbefore a background run will attempt them again. The scheduler can also expire\nstale running production leases through guarded compare/write preconditions,\nturning interrupted jobs into retryable review states while preserving\nheartbeat-refresh conflicts. Each run can persist a\n<code>production_scheduler_report.json</code> bound to the final production status so\nUI/agent layers can show completed outputs, retry conflicts, blocked work,\nexpired leases, lease conflicts, and failure messages without rerunning\norchestration. Schema v3 reports now also carry observe-only\n<code>workflow_authority</code> plus derived product metrics so pilot analytics can track\nthroughput and intervention rate from the trusted handoff without turning the\nhandoff into file-operation authority. Stage-specific local adapters now\ndeclare output-kind capabilities in the adapter registry, and the scheduler\nuses that registry for both worker planning and stale-lease expiration:\n<code>proxy-production-local</code> receives only <code>proxy_media</code> jobs and\n<code>analysis-production-local</code> receives only <code>vlm_asset_analysis</code> jobs.\n<code>scene-production-local</code> receives only <code>scene_grouping</code> jobs and writes the\nfirst deterministic serial rejoin artifact from trusted analysis outputs.\n<code>look-production-local</code> receives only <code>look_development</code> jobs and writes a\ndeterministic shoot-look profile from the verified scene summary.\n<code>grade-production-local</code> receives only <code>graded_photo</code>/<code>graded_video</code> jobs and\nwrites deterministic stand-in graded artifacts from one trusted original plus\nschema-validated/checksum-verified analysis and look dependencies.\n<code>story-production-local</code> receives only <code>storyline_selection</code> jobs and writes\ndeterministic schema v2 storyline selections from checksum-verified analysis,\nscene, look, and graded inputs. <code>package-production-local</code> receives only\n<code>instagram_reel</code>, <code>instagram_carousel</code>, and <code>instagram_photo_set</code> jobs, proving\npackage handoff and directory-output checksums before real render/export\npackage workers are trusted.</li>\n<li>A workspace health/index handoff that summarizes trusted artifacts and review\nstate for Mac app shells, background agents, and continuation runs without\ngranting new media-write or deletion authority. It now covers production\nstatus and production scheduler reports as well as render handoffs, so\npre-render progress, retryable conflicts, blocked jobs, and next safe actions\nare visible without custom manifest parsing. Workspace health schema v4 and\nworkspace index schema v2 carry the shared observe-only <code>workflow_authority</code>\ncontract so native UI and agent layers can separate presentation/diagnostic\nstate from permission to copy, retry, materialize, overwrite, clean up, or\ndelete files.</li>\n<li>Schema v2 CLI handoff summaries/receipts for <code>plan-import-route</code>,\n<code>preview-ingest</code>, <code>execute-ingest</code>, <code>plan-production</code>,\n<code>next-production-wave</code>, <code>write-render-tasks</code>, <code>card-dump-workflow</code>,\nrender-workspace inspection, and no-real-media demo creation. These payloads\nmay include next actions or <code>agent_handoff</code> review hints, but write-capable\nnext actions are command-free and the root <code>workflow_authority</code> object keeps\nthem presentation-only until a separate explicit command invocation supplies\nits confirmation/runtime arguments.</li>\n<li>A read-only pilot dashboard contract that consumes workspace health and\nvalidated scheduler product metrics to show activation, throughput, and manual\nintervention signals without parsing raw worker internals or granting copy,\nretry, cleanup, overwrite, materialization, or deletion authority.</li>\n<li>A read-only pilot cohort report that aggregates saved dashboard JSON payloads\ninto pilot-ready workspace rate, median intervention rate, and first-draft\noutput count so pilot operations can measure activation quality without\nspreadsheets or raw worker-log parsing.</li>\n<li>A pilot cohort demo fixture that creates multiple trusted no-real-media demo\nworkspaces, saves one pilot-dashboard JSON payload per workspace, and writes a\nsaved <code>pilot_cohort_report.json</code> so GTM demos can show cohort readiness without\nspreadsheets, real customer media, or raw worker-log parsing.</li>\n<li>A pilot cohort brief contract that reads the saved cohort report and emits\npresentation-ready readiness/intervention/throughput labels, structured\nblocker counts, and controlled per-workspace blocker labels for native shells\nand GTM demos without exposing workflow commands. Its optional text output\ngives demo shells a readable cohort view while JSON remains the default\nintegration contract.</li>\n<li>A package handoff brief contract that reads the trusted production status and\nscheduler report from an ingest manifest, summarizes package job readiness and\nmaterialized package outputs for native shells, and returns disabled\ncopy/retry/materialization controls from the report authority rather than\nreport prose.</li>\n<li>Parallelized analysis and grading plan contracts.</li>\n<li>Deterministic reel/carousel/photo-set assembly contracts.</li>\n<li>A <code>write-render-tasks</code> CLI handoff that turns trusted storyline selections and\ngraded artifacts into <code>deliverables/render_tasks.json</code> from the manifest-backed\nproduction plan, while refusing to overwrite a different existing handoff and\nemitting observe-only root authority on its handoff summary.</li>\n<li>Safe render-status initialization plus dry-run worker scheduler/status\nreporting for resumable pipelines. Persisted render scheduler reports now carry\nobserve-only <code>workflow_authority</code> alongside validated product metrics, keeping\nscheduler evidence separate from any future retry/materialization authority.</li>\n<li>Read-only render-workspace inspection that tells a Mac app, launch agent, or\ncontinuation automation whether to initialize, schedule, review blocked or\nretryable work, or review deliverables without mutating files; the summary now\ncarries the same root no-authority contract as workspace health.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Phase 2: productionized deliverables</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Real renderer adapters (ffmpeg/Core Image/Metal/Resolve workflows), including\nreplacing the deterministic grade stand-in with real color-rendered media.</li>\n<li>Visual review UI for selects, grade feedback, and retry controls.</li>\n<li>Better look transfer and style consistency controls.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Phase 3: workflow expansion</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>iPhone companion (review, approve, annotate, publish prep).</li>\n<li>Team workflows, client approvals, and shared review artifacts.</li>\n<li>Optional burst compute add-ons for speed-sensitive jobs.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>4) Monetization model</h2>\n<p>Use hybrid subscription + usage:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Starter / Solo:</strong> local-first ingestion + baseline automation.</li>\n<li><strong>Pro:</strong> higher throughput, stronger preset/look controls, collaboration.</li>\n<li><strong>Usage Boost:</strong> optional accelerated processing/render credits for\nexceptionally large jobs.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Pricing anchor should be ROI vs:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>editor spend replaced/reduced,</li>\n<li>hours reclaimed per week,</li>\n<li>faster client turnaround and higher retained capacity.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>5) Go-to-market plan</h2>\n<h2>Channel strategy</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Primary:</strong> Instagram-native demand capture (short demos of workflow speed,\nquality consistency, and output volume).</li>\n<li><strong>Secondary:</strong> creator/photo education partners and professional communities.</li>\n<li><strong>Direct outreach:</strong> targeted outreach to studio owners and high-volume\nfreelancers.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Messaging strategy</h2>\n<p>Lead with proof:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>&quot;No destructive ingest.&quot;</li>\n<li>&quot;Deterministic workflow with resumable jobs.&quot;</li>\n<li>&quot;More deliverables per week from the same footage.&quot;</li>\n<li>&quot;Hours saved and turnaround reduced.&quot;</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Avoid guarantees:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>no guaranteed virality claims,</li>\n<li>no guaranteed revenue outcomes,</li>\n<li>no &quot;one-click perfect edit&quot; promises.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>6) Success metrics</h2>\n<p>Track product and business metrics together:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>median ingest-to-first-draft time,</li>\n<li>median hours saved/user/week (self-reported + modeled),</li>\n<li>deliverables generated per shoot,</li>\n<li>manual intervention rate per 100 tasks,</li>\n<li>pilot-ready workspace rate from trusted dashboard thresholds (default: &gt;=90%\ncompletion, &lt;=20% manual intervention, and &gt;=1 materialized output),</li>\n<li>pilot readiness blocker mix from cohort reports: missing trusted metrics,\ncompletion below threshold, intervention above threshold, or missing\nfirst-draft outputs,</li>\n<li>paid conversion from trial,</li>\n<li>retention at 30/90 days,</li>\n<li>expansion (seat upgrades or usage add-ons).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>6.1) Unit-economics guardrails (working assumptions)</h2>\n<p>Use pricing and packaging that stays obviously ROI-positive for the pro ICP:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>If a customer saves even 6-10 hours/week, price can be anchored against\nrecovered billable time and reduced editor coordination.</li>\n<li>For customers currently spending $100-$1,000+/week on editing/coordination,\nsoftware pricing should target a clear fraction of that spend, while proving\nbetter throughput and consistency.</li>\n<li>Optional compute add-ons should be margin-protected and transparent; local-first\ndefaults reduce cloud cost volatility and preserve trust with large datasets.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>6.2) Validation experiments before broad scale</h2>\n<p>Run practical experiments tied to this ICP-first plan:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Workflow proof demos:</strong> show end-to-end &quot;card dump -&gt; graded social draft&quot;\nwith concrete turnaround deltas and safety notes.</li>\n<li><strong>Instagram demand tests:</strong> short-form before/after process ads targeted to\nwedding/event/photo-video professionals.</li>\n<li><strong>Problem-interview loop:</strong> weekly interviews with active pros to validate\ntop blockers (ingest risk, quality consistency, revision overhead).</li>\n<li><strong>Pilot cohort pricing tests:</strong> test one base plan + one pro plan + optional\nburst compute credits with usage telemetry.</li>\n<li><strong>Quality confidence metric:</strong> track how often users accept default selects/\ngrades/deliverables vs requiring manual intervention.</li>\n<li><strong>Pilot readiness gate:</strong> count a shoot as dashboard-ready only from the\nschema v2 <code>pilot_acceptance</code> payload, not from raw worker logs or manual\nspreadsheet interpretation.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>7) Key risks and mitigations</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Risk:</strong> perceived output quality is inconsistent.<ul>\n<li><strong>Mitigation:</strong> prioritize deterministic scene/look consistency controls and\nreview loops before broad generative features.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Risk:</strong> trust breaks due to file safety concern.<ul>\n<li><strong>Mitigation:</strong> preserve strict no-delete/no-overwrite rules and make safety\nevidence visible in UI and docs.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Risk:</strong> support load from too-broad audience early.<ul>\n<li><strong>Mitigation:</strong> enforce clear ICP focus on pro recurring workflows first.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Risk:</strong> cloud cost creep for heavy jobs.<ul>\n<li><strong>Mitigation:</strong> keep local-first default and meter optional burst compute.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>8) Execution priorities for next iteration</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Bind native Mac metadata and UI approval around the safe route recommendation\nand ingest assistant flow. The core now has both portable mounted-volume\ndiscovery and a typed macOS metadata adapter; the <code>plan-import-route</code> +\n<code>preview-ingest</code> + <code>execute-ingest --confirm</code> CLI commands expose the full\noperator-review-then-copy path, and <code>plan-production</code> exposes the next\nread-only post-ingest summary. The <code>card-dump-workflow</code> command combines\nthose steps into one native-shell contract, so the next step is binding it to\na SwiftUI/menu-bar approval screen before AI/color work starts.</li>\n<li>Extend the post-ingest report toward native UI proof. The render-task half\nnow exists in both <code>shootflow.demo_workspace</code> and the real\n<code>write-render-tasks</code> CLI handoff, and the synthetic card-dump demo now runs\nfrom detected card to checksum ingest, persisted render tasks, status\ninitialization, scheduler report, and reviewable outputs. <code>index-workspace</code>\nprovides the UI/agent state snapshot and <code>inspect-render-workspace</code> provides\nthe safe read-only state probe before initialization and after scheduler runs.</li>\n<li>Extend deterministic production probes toward real quality workers: replace\nthe proxy stand-in with ffmpeg/Core Image/Metal downsampled proxy generation,\nreplace <code>analysis-production-local</code> with a local or hosted VLM adapter, and\nreplace <code>scene-production-local</code>/<code>look-production-local</code> with real scene\nclustering and color-look context, and replace <code>grade-production-local</code> with\nffmpeg/Core Image/Metal grading behind the same no-delete/no-overwrite,\ndeclared-output-only rules. Replace <code>story-production-local</code> with a real\neditorial/story intelligence worker behind the same checksum-verified input\nand declared-output-only boundary.</li>\n<li>Build a minimal review loop UI contract (approve, retry, tweak grade intent).</li>\n<li>Bind the pilot-dashboard contract into the future Mac UI, continuation\ndashboards, and GTM demos so throughput, manual intervention, lease conflicts,\nreview-required rates, and schema v2 pilot-readiness thresholds become visible\nfrom trusted handoff metrics. Use the structured <code>workflow_authority</code> JSON\nblock from dashboards, cohort reports, and cohort briefs as the native UI&#39;s\nfirst safety gate before exposing any adjacent file-changing controls.</li>\n<li>Use the saved pilot cohort demo fixture for proof-based GTM content while\nreal pilot workspaces are still scarce; the demo should show readiness\nthresholds and safety boundaries, not imply automatic publishing or cleanup.</li>\n<li>Start proof-based GTM content showing real workflows and outcomes.</li>\n</ol>\n";

